  "term": "incidental memory",
  "definition": "In cognition, incidental memory refers to memory measured for material encountered without prior knowledge that it would later be tested, such as in a surprise recognition task. In the source packet, it is contrasted with intentional memory conditions in which participants know a subsequent memory test is coming.",
